feat(touch): probe GCC and GENI read-only, and gate bring-up behind TOUCH?

The first QUPv3 boot on this tree printed the SE revision, muxed pins 36/37
to qup13, pulsed reset, and then stopped: the next line would have come from
kt_se_init(), which writes the GENI block, and the USB console never came
back.  That run says nothing about I2C itself; it says the first GENI write
is where the board stops being observable.

Make every hardware step explicit and conservative:

  - add a read-only GCC probe for the three SE13 clocks the vendor DTS names
    (GCC_QUPV3_WRAP1_S5_CLK, GCC_QUPV3_WRAP_1_M_AHB_CLK and ..._S_AHB_CLK)
    with the offsets and bits from gcc-kona.c, through two 4 KiB pages
    rather than the 2 MiB GCC block;
  - add a read-only GENI/TLMM dump: QUP_HW_VER, firmware revision,
    GENI_STATUS, master/slave IRQ status, DMA mode, CGC control, SCL
    counters, FIFO status and the four pins;
  - stop running the driver at boot.  kebab_touch=1 now maps MMIO and
    prints a hint; the hardware is untouched unless kebab_touch_boot=1 asks
    for the old behaviour or kebab_touch_probe=1 asks for the read-only
    dump;
  - add TOUCH? (probe) and TOUCHINIT (pins, reset, se_init, identify) to the
    USB console, so a bad GENI access costs only the console it was typed
    into, not the boot path;
  - trace kt_se_init() before each register group it writes, so a hang names
    the group.

No transfer, clock enable, firmware update or reset change is added here:
this patch only makes the next experiment observable.

